#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:4
msgid "PD separation"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:6
msgid ""
"Prefill/Decode (PD) separation is available in the community edition. "
"Prefill replicas compute prompt KV cache; decode replicas reuse it through "
"Xavier or native NIXL and produce the response. Requests are scheduled "
"round-robin within each role. No enterprise package or License is required."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:12
msgid "Launch"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:14
msgid ""
"Xavier requires NVIDIA GPUs, a reachable host address (not ``0.0.0.0``), and"
" vLLM 0.21.0 or newer. Older deployments can use the legacy Xavier "
"integration with vLLM below 0.11.0; versions 0.11 through 0.20 are not "
"supported."
msgstr ""
"Xavier requiere GPU NVIDIA, una dirección de host accesible (no ``0.0.0.0``)"
" y vLLM 0.21.0 o posterior. Las implementaciones antiguas pueden usar la "
"integración anterior de Xavier con vLLM inferior a 0.11.0; las versiones "
"0.11 a 0.20 no son compatibles."

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:19
msgid ""
"The example starts one prefill replica on GPU 0 and one decode replica on "
"GPU 1. Replace the worker address with the full ``ip:port`` reported by "
"``client.get_workers_info()``. Both replicas must use the same model and "
"engine configuration."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:51
msgid ""
"The same ``replica_config`` is accepted by ``POST /v1/models``, the async "
"Python client, and the CLI ``--replica_config`` JSON option. In the Web UI, "
"select vLLM, enable per-replica placement, and choose Prefill or Decode for "
"each replica. The community launch path defaults to Xavier when P/D roles "
"appear."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:57
msgid "CLI launch"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:59
msgid "Start a local server first, or use an existing supervisor endpoint:"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:65
msgid "In another terminal, launch a 1P+1D deployment:"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:78
msgid ""
"Replace ``WORKER_ADDRESS`` with the worker's registered address, including "
"its actor port (shown in the worker startup log), not the HTTP API port. For"
" workers on different machines, use each worker's own address and GPU "
"indices. ``--replica_config`` is an alias for ``--replica-config``. The "
"replica count is inferred from the array length; no separate Xavier switch "
"is needed. Do not combine per-replica placement with global ``--n-gpu``, "
"``--gpu-idx``, or ``--worker-ip``. Invalid PD roles or incomplete P/D "
"topology fail before the launch request is sent."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:88
msgid "Configuration rules"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:90
msgid ""
"``replica`` is the total number of P and D replicas. At least one of each "
"role is required; more than one of either role is supported."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:92
msgid ""
"Omitted roles default to ``hybrid`` (ordinary replicas). A PD deployment "
"cannot mix hybrid replicas with P/D replicas."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:94
msgid ""
"Each entry specifies one worker and its GPU allocation. Different replicas "
"may run on different workers. Per-replica placement cannot be combined with "
"global ``worker_ip``, ``gpu_idx`` or ``n_gpu``, or cross-worker sharding "
"within a replica (``n_worker > 1``)."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:98
msgid ""
"``vllm_transfer_backend_type`` (alias ``transfer_backend_type``) selects "
"``xavier`` (default) or ``nixl``. Unknown backend names are rejected."
msgstr ""
"``vllm_transfer_backend_type`` (alias ``transfer_backend_type``) selecciona "
"``xavier`` (predeterminado) o ``nixl``. Se rechazan los nombres de backend "
"desconocidos."

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:101
msgid ""
"The topology is fixed for the deployment lifetime. To change its size or "
"roles, terminate the model and relaunch it with the new configuration."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:105
msgid "Inference and lifecycle"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:107
msgid ""
"Send OpenAI-compatible chat/completion requests to the model UID used at "
"launch. Both streaming and non-streaming responses are supported. Wait for "
"all replicas to be ready before sending requests. Aborting a request stops "
"work on both roles; terminating the model releases the deployment resources."
msgstr ""
"Envíe solicitudes de chat/completado compatibles con OpenAI al UID del "
"modelo utilizado al iniciar. Se admiten respuestas con y sin streaming. "
"Espere a que todas las réplicas estén listas. Cancelar una solicitud detiene"
" el trabajo de ambos roles; terminar el modelo libera los recursos del "
"despliegue."

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:134
msgid "Hybrid/recurrent attention limitation"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:136
msgid ""
"Xavier PD does not support hybrid/recurrent attention models such as "
"Qwen3.5. Deploy these models without PD, or choose a full-attention model "
"such as Qwen3 for PD."
msgstr ""
"Xavier PD no admite modelos de atención híbrida/recurrente como Qwen3.5. "
"Despliegue estos modelos sin PD o elija un modelo de atención completa como "
"Qwen3 para PD."

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:143
msgid "Xavier requirements and memory"
msgstr "Requisitos y memoria de Xavier"

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:145
msgid ""
"Xavier V1 requires one GPU per replica (TP=1, PP=1) and text-only models "
"without LoRA. Multimodal models, prompt embeddings and salted prompts are "
"not supported."
msgstr ""
"Xavier V1 requiere una GPU por réplica (TP=1, PP=1) y modelos de solo texto "
"sin LoRA. No admite modelos multimodales, embeddings de prompts ni prompts "
"con salt."

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:149
msgid ""
"Xavier's CPU cache can consume as much memory as the engine's GPU KV cache. "
"Allow additional host memory for transfers when sizing your deployment."
msgstr ""
"La caché de CPU de Xavier puede consumir tanta memoria como la caché KV de "
"GPU del motor. Reserve memoria adicional del host para las transferencias al"
" dimensionar el despliegue."

#: user_guide/pd_separation.rst:57
msgid "Native NIXL backend"
msgstr "Backend NIXL nativo"

#: user_guide/pd_separation.rst:57
msgid ""
"Set ``vllm_transfer_backend_type=\"nixl\"`` in the launch example to use "
"vLLM's native NixlConnector. Install ``nixl`` in the model environment "
"together with vLLM 0.21.0 or newer. The initial integration supports text-"
"only models without LoRA and requires TP=1, PP=1 and DP=1 per replica. "
"Multiple P and D replicas are supported. Xavier remains the default backend."
msgstr ""
"Establezca ``vllm_transfer_backend_type=\"nixl\"`` en el ejemplo de inicio "
"para usar NixlConnector nativo de vLLM. Instale ``nixl`` junto con vLLM "
"0.21.0 o posterior en el entorno del modelo. La integración inicial admite "
"modelos de texto sin LoRA, requiere TP=1, PP=1 y DP=1 por réplica y permite "
"varias réplicas P y D. Xavier sigue siendo el backend predeterminado."

#: user_guide/pd_separation.rst:66
msgid ""
"Native NIXL PD requires ``n=1`` per request; parallel sampling is not "
"supported."
msgstr ""
"PD con NIXL nativo requiere ``n=1`` por solicitud; no admite muestreo "
"paralelo."

msgid ""
"For NIXL, wildcard worker binds are supported through automatic host "
"discovery. Set ``VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_HOST`` in launch ``envs`` or the "
"worker environment to select a reachable interface; launch ``envs`` take "
"precedence. If discovery fails or returns loopback, configure this variable "
"explicitly. Xinference always replaces ``VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_PORT`` with "
"a dynamically allocated port per replica, including on recovery. A fixed "
"side-channel port is not supported; firewalls must allow dynamic ports "
"between replica hosts."
msgstr ""
"NIXL admite enlaces comodín del worker mediante detección automática del "
"host. Defina ``VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_HOST`` en los ``envs`` de inicio o en "
"el entorno del worker para elegir una interfaz accesible; los ``envs`` de "
"inicio tienen prioridad. Si falla la detección o devuelve loopback, "
"configure esta variable explícitamente. Xinference siempre reemplaza "
"``VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_PORT`` por un puerto dinámico por réplica, también "
"durante la recuperación. No se admiten puertos fijos; los cortafuegos deben "
"permitir puertos dinámicos entre los hosts de las réplicas."

msgid "After a worker restart, relaunch the native NIXL PD deployment."
msgstr ""
"Tras reiniciar un worker, vuelva a iniciar el despliegue PD con NIXL nativo."

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:203
msgid "GPU-first Xavier cache (experimental)"
msgstr "Caché Xavier con prioridad GPU (experimental)"

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:206
msgid ""
"For the Xavier backend, set ``xavier_gpu_cache_bytes`` to a non-negative "
"integer, such as ``268435456`` for 256 MiB per replica. Omit it to use the "
"existing CPU cache, or set it to ``0`` to use GPU-first caching with no GPU "
"storage budget. This option does not select the native vLLM NIXL backend."
msgstr ""
"Con el backend Xavier, establezca ``xavier_gpu_cache_bytes`` en un entero no"
" negativo, por ejemplo ``268435456`` para 256 MiB por réplica. Omítalo para "
"usar la caché CPU existente o use ``0`` para activar la caché con prioridad "
"GPU sin presupuesto de almacenamiento GPU. Esta opción no selecciona el "
"backend NIXL nativo de vLLM."

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:208
msgid ""
"Install ``xoscar[nixl]>=0.11.1`` in both the worker and model environments. "
"GPU-first caching requires Linux, NVIDIA CUDA, vLLM 0.21.0 or newer, a full-"
"attention model and one GPU per replica (TP=1, PP=1). Use the same model, "
"cache dtype and engine configuration on all replicas."
msgstr ""
"Instale ``xoscar[nixl]>=0.11.1`` tanto en el entorno del worker como en el "
"del modelo. La caché con prioridad GPU requiere Linux, NVIDIA CUDA, vLLM "
"0.21.0 o posterior, un modelo de atención completa y una GPU por réplica "
"(TP=1, PP=1). Use el mismo modelo, tipo de datos de caché y configuración "
"del motor en todas las réplicas."

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:210
msgid ""
"The budget applies only to Xavier's GPU cache. Leave additional GPU memory "
"for the model, vLLM's own KV cache and transfers. When this cache fills, "
"Xavier stores reusable data in CPU memory; if no cache space is available, "
"new data may not be retained for reuse."
msgstr ""
"El presupuesto solo se aplica a la caché GPU de Xavier. Reserve memoria GPU "
"adicional para el modelo, la propia caché KV de vLLM y las transferencias. "
"Cuando esta caché se llena, Xavier guarda datos reutilizables en la memoria "
"CPU; si no hay espacio disponible, es posible que los datos nuevos no se "
"conserven para reutilizarlos."

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst
msgid "GPU-first caching requires the Xavier backend and more than one replica."
msgstr "La caché con prioridad de GPU requiere el backend Xavier y más de una réplica."

#: user_guide/pd_separation.rst:211
msgid ""
"With GPU-first caching, cache transfers can overlap with response generation"
" for other requests."
msgstr ""
"Con la caché con prioridad GPU, las transferencias de caché pueden solaparse"
" con la generación de respuestas de otras solicitudes."

msgid ""
"For implementation details, profiling and contributor tests, see the `Xavier"
" developer README "
"<https://github.com/xorbitsai/inference/blob/main/xinference/model/llm/vllm/xavier/README.md>`_."
msgstr ""
"Para detalles de implementación, profiling y pruebas de desarrollo, consulte"
" `Xavier developer README "
"<https://github.com/xorbitsai/inference/blob/main/xinference/model/llm/vllm/xavier/README.md>`_."

#: ../../source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:145
msgid "Transfer failures and incompatible KV cache layouts raise errors instead of silently recomputing the request."
msgstr "Los fallos de transferencia y los formatos de caché KV incompatibles generan errores en lugar de volver a calcular la solicitud silenciosamente."
